What:   lets shpool's own tests run on macOS where they were skipped for reasons of the tests,
        not of shpool. The zsh and fish tests named /usr/bin/zsh and /usr/bin/fish (macOS has
        /bin/zsh, and homebrew's fish is elsewhere); they now find the shell on $PATH and in the
        usual places (support::find_shell, support::shell_config), and say so if it is not
        installed. The four motd pager tests, skipped for a "pager pty output issue", pass on
        macOS now and are no longer skipped.
Where:  shpool/tests only: attach.rs, support/mod.rs, and the three configs that named a shell
        path, which become templates (data/*.toml -> data/*.toml.tmpl).
Shape:  tests only; shpool itself is unchanged.
Needs:  01-rename.patch before it (cut against its result).
Status: to be offered upstream (shell-pool/shpool).

